e><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Herfarth</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Gagliardi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Swanson</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name><name><surname>Birnbaum</surname><given-names>EH</given-names></name><name><surname>Read</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name><name><surname>Fleshman</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Kodner</surname><given-names>IJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Moley</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Confirmation that chromosome 18q allelic loss in colon cancer is a prognostic indicator</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>1998</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>427</fpage><lpage>433</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9469325</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhou</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodman</surname><given-names>SN</given-names></name><name><surname>Galizia</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Lieto</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferraraccio</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Pignatelli</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Purdie</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Piris</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Morris</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Harrison</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Paty</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name><name><surname>Culliford</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Romans</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Montgomery</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name><name><surname>Choti</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kinzler</surna